# colord -- the system colour management daemon.
#
# gnome-control-center's Colour panel and gnome-settings-daemon's colour plugin
# both talk to it over D-Bus, and gnome-settings-daemon is what applies an ICC
# profile to a display at login. Without colord the panel is inert and no
# calibration is ever loaded.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env. BLFS
# 12.4 carries 1.4.8.
SRC_URL=https://www.freedesktop.org/software/colord/releases/colord-1.4.8.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=21500bd68975312a7f0f3ce6019d9f75f42aacaa75ca7115ec720b5445406896
SRC_DIR=colord-1.4.8

# -Ddaemon_user=colord IS THE MOST IMPORTANT FLAG HERE AND ITS DEFAULT IS root.
#
# meson_options.txt line: option('daemon_user', type : 'string', value : 'root').
# Upstream knows this is wrong and meson.build 196-197 says so:
#
#   if get_option('daemon_user') == 'root'
#     warning('RUNNING THE DAEMON AS root IS NOT A GOOD IDEA, use -Ddaemon_user= to set user')
#
# A WARNING, NOT AN ERROR. So the default builds cleanly, installs cleanly, and
# ships a system D-Bus service that runs colord as root -- while
# duct-filesystem's passwd template has carried a colord account at uid 71 all
# along, unused. The account existing and the daemon using it are separate
# facts, and only the second one is worth anything; install.sh asserts the
# second rather than trusting this flag.
#
# The value reaches three installed files, which is why it is worth getting
# right in one place: the D-Bus activation file (User=), the D-Bus policy
# (<policy user=>), and the udev rules (rules/meson.build:2).
#
# -Dsystemd=false. UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS TRUE. Duct has elogind and no systemd,
# and this is the flag that decides whether a systemd unit and its sysusers.conf
# are installed. Note that colord.sysusers.conf would be the systemd way of
# creating the colord user -- irrelevant here for two reasons: it is off, and
# tape has no install hooks to run anything like it. The account comes from
# duct-filesystem's passwd/group templates instead.
#
# -Dbash_completion=false: UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS TRUE and it needs the
# bash-completion framework, which is a separate project and is not packaged.
# The same default failed dconf's configure outright.
#
# -Dargyllcms_sensor=false: UPSTREAM DEFAULT IS TRUE. It wants ArgyllCMS's
# spotread. meson.build:178 takes it required:false so this would not fail --
# but a soft-skip that happens to do what is wanted is not a decision, and BLFS
# pins it off too.
#
# -Dman=false and -Ddocs=false: both default TRUE and both need the DocBook XSL
# stylesheets, which are not packaged anywhere in this tree -- the same call
# libnotify, kmod, eudev, elogind, ostree, linux-pam, wayland, dconf and flatpak
# have each already made. libxslt provides xsltproc; it does NOT provide the
# stylesheets, and that distinction cost this chain a CI cycle on libnotify.
#
# TWO DELIBERATE DIVERGENCES FROM THE BLFS COMMAND LINE, both because the thing
# it assumes is not packaged here:
#
#   -Dvapi=false           BLFS passes -D vapi=true. That needs vala, which is
#                          not in this tree. Left at its upstream default of
#                          false.
#   -Dlibcolordcompat=false
#                          BLFS passes -D libcolordcompat=true, which exists to
#                          support ArgyllCMS. ArgyllCMS is not packaged and the
#                          sensor support above is off, so the compatibility
#                          shim would have no consumer. Upstream default.
#
# NOT SET, deliberately:
#
#   -Dudev_rules   left at its default of true. It needs dependency('udev')
#                  (meson.build:126), and eudev DOES provide udev.pc -- checked
#                  in the 3.2.14 tarball, which ships both src/udev/udev.pc.in
#                  and src/libudev/libudev.pc.in. Recorded because "the udev
#                  package is called eudev here" is exactly the kind of thing
#                  that looks like a missing dependency at a glance.
#   -Dintrospection
#                  left at its default of true; gobject-introspection is
#                  packaged and the Colord typelib is what the Settings panel's
#                  JavaScript reaches it through.
#   -Dsane, -Dprint_profiles, -Dsession_example, -Dinstalled_tests
#                  all already false upstream. Recorded rather than passed, so a
#                  future default flip is visible as a change rather than as a
#                  silent new dependency.
MESON_ARGS="-Ddaemon_user=colord -Dsystemd=false -Dbash_completion=false \
-Dargyllcms_sensor=false -Dman=false -Ddocs=false \
-Dvapi=false -Dlibcolordcompat=false"
